Description: Evaluates model-written code in the calling environment of a
    running 'R' session, so agents work on objects already in memory instead
    of reloading data from files or rerunning scripts. One function, peter(),
    opens a chat in the console or, given a prompt, calls either kind of
    model: typed decision models (System 1) return logical, character or
    numeric vectors with probabilities, and conversational models (System 2)
    run as tool-using agents. Conversational models come from the 'Anthropic'
    <https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/overview>, 'OpenAI'
    <https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/overview> and
    'Google Gemini' <https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs> APIs,
    'OpenAI'-compatible endpoints, local 'Ollama' <https://ollama.com> models
    and the 'Claude Code' and 'Codex' command line tools; decision models
    include 'Jev', hosted by 'TypeSafe AI'
    <https://docs.typesafe.ai/introduction>, and the local 'Clef'. For
    reproducible research, top-level peter() calls can be recorded, with the
    code they ran, in 'R' scripts, 'R Markdown' and 'Quarto' documents or
    'Jupyter' notebooks; with the same data and packages, a recorded script
    replays without a model or keys, or reruns with another model.
